.. list-table:: Pass properties
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 16 26 12 46

   * - Property
     - Accepted values
     - Backends
     - Meaning
   * - ``name``
     - DSL identifier
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Legacy only: the pass name. In version 2 the key of the pass is its name, a DSL identifier.
   * - ``program``
     - nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Required. The program the pass runs: ``glsl/<program>.glsl``, or ``glsl/<program>.vert`` with ``glsl/<program>.frag``, and ``wgsl/<program>.wgsl`` (Section 8.1).
   * - ``type``
     - ``"render"``, ``"compute"``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Labels the pass. WebGPU chooses compute or render from the ``@compute`` or ``@fragment`` entry in the WGSL source.
   * - ``entryPoint``
     - nonempty string
     - WebGPU
     - The compute entry point. An entry point found in the source takes precedence. WebGL2 and WebGPU render passes ignore it.
   * - ``drawMode``
     - ``"points"``, ``"triangles"``, ``"billboards"``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Draws ``points``, ``billboards`` (one quad for each instance) or ``triangles`` (with a depth test, back-face culling and depth cleared for each pass). Without it the pass draws one full-screen triangle.
   * - ``drawBuffers``
     - positive integer
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - More than one selects the multiple render target path. The attachments follow the order of the ``outputs`` keys.
   * - ``count``
     - positive integer; or ``"auto"``, ``"screen"``, ``"input"``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - The vertex or instance count. ``auto`` and ``screen`` use the size of the output texture. ``input`` uses the size of ``xyzTex`` or ``inputTex`` for points, ``xyzTex`` for billboards, and ``meshPositions`` or ``inputTex`` for triangles.
   * - ``countUniform``
     - nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Triangles only: a declared global whose value, when above 0, sets the count.
   * - ``repeat``
     - positive integer; or nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Runs the pass this many times in each frame: an integer, or a uniform name that resolves to one.
   * - ``blend``
     - boolean; or array of 2 items, each: nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - ``true`` blends additively (one, one). ``[src, dst]`` names the two blend factors.
   * - ``workgroups``
     - array of 1 to 3 items, each: positive integer
     - WebGPU
     - The compute dispatch size in workgroups, for each dimension. A legacy definition may also give a uniform name, which has no effect; version 2 refuses one.
   * - ``storageBuffers``
     - refused in version 2
     - none
     - Legacy only. It has no effect: the WebGPU backend allocates storage buffers from the shader bindings. Version 2 refuses it.
   * - ``storageTextures``
     - object of names to: nonempty string
     - WebGPU
     - WGSL storage binding name to the texture a compute pass writes. Only ``outputTex`` writes today (Limitations below).
   * - ``viewport``
     - object with ``x``, ``y``, ``w``, ``h``, ``width``, ``height``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - The pass region: ``x``, ``y``, ``w`` and ``h`` in pixels, or ``width`` and ``height`` in the size grammar. When the pass writes a texture, both backends render to the full size of that texture.
   * - ``conditions``
     - object with ``runIf``, ``skipIf``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - ``runIf`` and ``skipIf``: lists of ``{ "uniform", "equals" }``. Each compares a declared global with its value by strict equality, each frame.
   * - ``defines``
     - object of names to: string; or number
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Preprocessor definitions. The pass runs its own build of its program with them.
   * - ``uniforms``
     - object of names to: number; or nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Shader uniform to a global name, or to a numeric literal.
   * - ``inputs``
     - object of names to: nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Sampler name to texture: a pipeline input (``inputTex``, ``inputTex3d``, ``inputGeo``, ``inputXyz``, ``inputVel``, ``inputRgba``, ``inputColor``, ``midiNoteGrid``, ``feedback``, ``selfTex``, ``outputTex``, ``none``), ``o0`` to ``o7``, a ``global_`` surface, a declared texture, a global, or the ``externalTexture`` name. Version 2 refuses ``noise``, which nothing writes.
   * - ``outputs``
     - object of names to: nonempty string
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Fragment output to texture: a pipeline output (``outputTex``, ``outputTex3d``, ``outputXyz``, ``outputVel``, ``outputRgba``, ``inputTex3d``, ``inputGeo``, ``inputXyz``, ``inputVel``, ``inputRgba``), a ``feedback_`` texture, a ``global_`` surface, or a declared texture. Writing to a chain input writes the value back to it.
   * - ``clear``
     - boolean
     - WebGPU
     - Clears the target before the pass. WebGL2 effect passes do not clear.
   * - ``samplerTypes``
     - object of names to: ``"default"``, ``"nearest"``, ``"repeat"``, ``"mipmap"``
     - WebGPU
     - WGSL sampler binding name to ``default`` (linear), ``nearest``, ``repeat`` or ``mipmap``. Without it WebGPU samples nearest, an uploaded texture with ``default``, a mipmapped input with ``mipmap`` and a 3D input with its filter. WebGL2 samples 2D textures nearest, and mipmapped textures with linear mipmap filtering.

.. list-table:: Resource forms
   :header-rows: 1
   :widths: 16 22 14 48

   * - Form
     - Declared by
     - Backends
     - Meaning
   * - ``texture``
     - ``textures``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - A 2D texture. The size is a number, ``screen``, ``auto``, ``input`` or ``resolution`` (the screen size), a percentage, or a size object (Section 8.6). A size that is not a plain number is resolved again when the canvas resizes. The format defaults to ``rgba16f``.
   * - ``persistentTexture``
     - ``persistent: true``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Keeps the contents when the texture is created again at a new size, and through a simulation reset.
   * - ``mipmappedTexture``
     - ``mipmaps: true``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Allocates a mip chain, which the pipeline generates again after each render. A simulation step may not sample it.
   * - ``volumeTexture``
     - ``textures3d``
     - WebGPU writes, WebGL2 samples
     - A 3D texture. ``depth`` defaults to the width, and ``filter`` to ``linear``. WebGL2 creates no framebuffer for a 3D texture: it can sample one but not write one.
   * - ``volumeAtlas``
     - ``outputTex3d`` and a ``volumeSize`` global
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - A volume stored as a 2D atlas, sized with ``{ "param": "volumeSize" }`` by ``{ "param": "volumeSize", "power": 2 }``. ``outputTex3d`` hands it on to the next effect, and ``volumeSize`` passes down the chain. The size is clamped to the device limit.
   * - ``geometry``
     - ``outputGeo``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - A geometry buffer that ``outputGeo`` hands on to the next effect. ``"inputGeo"`` passes the incoming buffer through.
   * - ``particleState``
     - ``textures.global_xyz``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Particle state shared by the effects of one chain: ``global_xyz``, ``global_vel`` and ``global_rgba``. These surfaces keep their bindings from frame to frame instead of swapping.
   * - ``multipleRenderTargets``
     - several ``outputs`` and ``drawBuffers``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - One pass writes several textures. When the colour attachments exceed the device budget, trailing ``rgba32f`` attachments are allocated as ``rgba16f``.
   * - ``storageTexture``
     - ``storageTextures``
     - WebGPU
     - A texture that a WebGPU compute pass writes through a storage binding.
   * - ``globalSurface``
     - ``o0`` to ``o7``, ``global_<name>``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Surfaces that every effect shares, double-buffered. ``o0`` to ``o7``, ``geo0`` to ``geo7`` and ``vol0`` to ``vol7`` always exist, and a ``global_`` surface exists once a pass names it. An ``oN`` input reads the chain input.
   * - ``meshSurface``
     - ``global_mesh<N>_positions``, ``_normals``, ``_uvs``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - The vertex data of ``mesh0`` to ``mesh7``, which the host fills with ``loadOBJFromURL()`` or ``loadOBJFromString()``. A triangles pass reads them by ``texelFetch``.
   * - ``hostTexture``
     - ``midiNoteGrid``, ``externalTexture``
     - WebGL2, WebGPU
     - Data the host uploads: the MIDI note grid each frame, and the media texture that ``externalTexture`` names, through ``updateTextureFromSource()``.
   * - ``sampler``
     - ``samplerTypes``
     - WebGPU
     - The sampler of a sampled WGSL input (see ``samplerTypes``).
